{
  "about": [
    "Quiz grading cases shared by the frontend (src/lib/quiz/grade.ts, checked by scripts/tests/quiz.test.ts) and the backend (app/core/quiz_kinds.py, its parity test reads a copy at tests/fixtures/quiz_grading_cases.json). Both files must stay byte-for-byte the same.",
    "items: wire questions by name, camelCase as the server sends them ({id, kind, question, options, correctAnswer, answer, explanation}).",
    "normalize: normalizeFill(input) == expected. Steps, in order: NFKC; lower case; trim; curly quotes to straight ones and U+2212 (minus) to '-'; strip . , ; : ! ? \" ' ( ) and whitespace from both ends; hyphens and dashes (U+002D, U+2010-U+2014) become spaces, except a '-' at the very start followed by a digit (a minus sign); collapse whitespace to one space and trim; drop one leading 'a ', 'an ' or 'the '.",
    "grade: grade(items[item], response) == expected {correct, right, total}. A response of the wrong kind is {correct: false, right: 0, total: parts}. single: choice == correctAnswer (1/1). true_false: value == answer.correct; a {kind: single} response is read as 0 = True, 1 = False (1/1). multi: the set of valid picked indices (integers in range, duplicates ignored) equals answer.correct; right = options judged right (picked and correct, or not picked and not correct), total = len(options). order / categorize / match: right = positions i < total where response[i] == answer.correct[i]; total = len(answer.correct) (order) or len(options); correct = right == total and len(response) == total. fill: normalise both; if both match ^-?(\\d+|\\d{1,3}(,\\d{3})+)(\\.\\d+)?$ compare as numbers (commas removed) with math.isclose(rel_tol=1e-6); else equal strings, or a restricted Damerau-Levenshtein distance <= 1 (counted in code points) when the accepted form is 5 or more code points long; 1/1.",
    "describe: answerText(item) / describe_answer and responseText(item, response) / describe_response (null = nothing to say)."
  ],
